摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"DeepSeek Harness plugin: OAuth / subscription-plan LLM providers (Grok, GitHub Copilot, OpenAI Codex, Anthropic, OpenRouter)","id":"gh:1333791759","install_available":true,"language":"TypeScript","name":"dsh-llm-oauth","slug":"ziyou979/dsh-llm-oauth","topics":["deepseek-harness","dsh-plugin","github-copilot","grok","oauth","openai-codex"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"DeepSeek Harness plugin: OAuth / subscription-plan LLM providers (Grok, GitHub Copilot, OpenAI Codex"},{"id":"p1s2","text":", Anthropic, OpenRouter)"},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# dsh-llm-oauth"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"English | 中文"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"Standalone **OAuth / subscription-plan** LLM plugin for DeepSeek Harness. Install it into your own p"},{"id":"p4s2","text":"rofile with `dsh plugin add` — it does **not** patch the Harness repo."},{"id":"p5s1","text":"Official `dsh-llm-pi-ai` authenticates with API keys only and never runs an OAuth login or refresh. "},{"id":"p5s2","text":"This plugin reuses the same catalog package, `@earendil-works/pi-ai`, but constructs `Models` with a"},{"id":"p5s3","text":" durable `CredentialStore` so subscription tokens refresh on the request path."},{"id":"p6s1","text":"Packaging follows the official plugin guides — your first plugin and publish / install:"},{"id":"p7s1","text":"- `package.json` → `dsh.bundle.patch` plus optional `dsh.client` (Web Settings face)\n- `cordis.patch"},{"id":"p7s2","text":".yml` inserts one plugin row\n- `prepare` bundles `src/` → `lib/` (including `lib/client.js`) on git "},{"id":"p7s3","text":"install\n- function plugin: export `name`, `inject`, `Config`, `apply` — **no `export default`**"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"## Providers"},{"id":"p9s1","text":"| Subscription | Provider id | Notes |"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"| Grok (SuperGrok / X Premium) | `xai` | Model ids come from the installed pi-ai catalog. |\n| GitHub"},{"id":"p10s2","text":" Copilot | `github-copilot` | Optional Enterprise URL defaults to public `github.com`. |\n| ChatGPT p"},{"id":"p10s3","text":"lan (current) | `openai` | **Sign in with ChatGPT** — the ChatGPT subscription through pi-ai's offic"},{"id":"p10s4","text":"ial flow (needs `@earendil-works/pi-ai` ≥ 1.0.0). Do not also configure an `openai` API key on the f"},{"id":"p10s5","text":"irst-party plugin: one route id takes one provider. |\n| ChatGPT / Codex plan (legacy) | `openai-code"},{"id":"p10s6","text":"x` | Device-code flow for the GPT-5.x Codex models. Needs device-code authorization enabled in ChatG"},{"id":"p10s7","text":"PT — see below. **Account-ban risk.** |\n| Anthropic subscription | `anthropic` | |\n| OpenRouter | `o"},{"id":"p10s8","text":"penrouter` | Large catalog — enable only if you need it. |\n| Kimi For Coding | `kimi-coding` | |"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"Model ids come from the installed `@earendil-works/pi-ai` catalog, not from this plugin. Bump that d"},{"id":"p11s2","text":"ependency and rebuild when you want a newer catalog."},{"id":"p12s1","text":"## Enable vs sign-in"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"After install the plugin is **dormant**: the catalog lists the providers above, but **`providers: {}"},{"id":"p13s2","text":"`**, so the model picker is **not** flooded with hundreds of models."},{"id":"p14s1","text":"| Concept | Meaning | How |"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"| **Enable** | Register the LLM route; provider appears in the picker | Settings → **OAuth / Subscri"},{"id":"p15s2","text":"ptions**, `/oauth enable xai`, or auto on login |\n| **Sign in** | Store tokens in `pi-ai-oauth.json`"},{"id":"p15s3","text":" | Settings panel, `/oauth login xai`, or `bin/login.mjs` |\n| **Disable** | Remove from picker; **ke"},{"id":"p15s4","text":"ep** stored tokens | Settings panel or `/oauth disable xai` |"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"Only **enabled** providers list models. They sit alongside API-key providers under Settings → **Mode"},{"id":"p16s2","text":"roviders list models. They sit alongside API-key providers under Settings → **Models** once enabled."},{"id":"p17s1","text":"## Install"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"From a local checkout:"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"Confirm the layer:"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p23s1","text":"A git install may ask you to allow `prepare` in the profile's `pnpm-workspace.yaml` (pnpm ≥10 refuse"},{"id":"p23s2","text":"s lifecycle scripts otherwise):"},{"id":"p24s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p25s1","text":"## Settings → OAuth / Subscriptions"},{"id":"p26s1","text":"The Web UI adds a settings section (between **Models** and **Plugins**) with:"},{"id":"p27s1","text":"- Every catalog subscription provider\n- Badges: enabled / disabled, signed-in / out, login-in-progre"},{"id":"p27s2","text":"ss\n- Actions: enable, disable, sign in, sign out (buttons on this page — no need to type `/oauth` in"},{"id":"p27s3","text":" chat)\n- Successful sign-in stores tokens and auto-enables the provider\n- Device codes show on the p"},{"id":"p27s4","text":"age (with copy); authorization URLs open in a new tab, or via **Open authorization page** if the pop"},{"id":"p27s5","text":"y); authorization URLs open in a new tab, or via **Open authorization page** if the popup is blocked"},{"id":"p28s1","text":"Providers that ask “pick a login method” (e.g. `openai-codex`) auto-select **device code** on Web."},{"id":"p29s1","text":"**Sign in with ChatGPT** (`openai`, pi-ai ≥ 1.0.0) starts pi-ai's callback server on the host at `12"},{"id":"p29s2","text":"7.0.0.1:1455`. If your browser runs on that machine the sign-in finishes by itself; when it cannot ("},{"id":"p29s3","text":"remote Web UI, port busy) the Settings page shows a **paste box** for the final redirect URL — from "},{"id":"p29s4","text":"chat, `/oauth code openai <redirect-url-or-code>` does the same."},{"id":"p30s1","text":"After a provider is enabled (and signed in), it also appears under Settings → **Models** next to API"},{"id":"p30s2","text":"ider is enabled (and signed in), it also appears under Settings → **Models** next to API-key routes:"},{"id":"p31s1","text":"API-key providers stay curated under **Settings → Models**. OAuth enable + login live on this plugin"},{"id":"p31s2","text":"providers stay curated under **Settings → Models**. OAuth enable + login live on this plugin’s page."},{"id":"p32s1","text":"Host HTTP API (same-origin Web):"},{"id":"p33s1","text":"| Method | Path | Body |"},{"id":"p34s1","text":"| `GET` | `/dsh-llm-oauth/status` | — |\n| `POST` | `/dsh-llm-oauth/enable` | `{ \"provider\": \"xai\" }`"},{"id":"p34s2","text":" |\n| `POST` | `/dsh-llm-oauth/disable` | `{ \"provider\": \"xai\" }` |\n| `POST` | `/dsh-llm-oauth/login`"},{"id":"p34s3","text":" | `{ \"provider\": \"xai\" }` |\n| `POST` | `/dsh-llm-oauth/code` | `{ \"provider\": \"openai\", \"code\": \"<r"},{"id":"p34s4","text":"edirect-url-or-code>\" }` |\n| `POST` | `/dsh-llm-oauth/logout` | `{ \"provider\": \"xai\" }` |"},{"id":"p35s1","text":"## ChatGPT: `openai` (current) vs `openai-codex` (legacy)"},{"id":"p36s1","text":"`openai` is pi-ai's **Sign in with ChatGPT** flow: the browser ends on the host's `127.0.0.1:1455` c"},{"id":"p36s2","text":"allback and the host exchanges the code. Nothing else to switch on, and no device-code toggle needed"},{"id":"p36s3","text":". When the callback cannot reach the host, paste the final redirect URL back (Settings page box, or "},{"id":"p36s4","text":"`/oauth code openai …`)."},{"id":"p37s1","text":"[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p38s1","text":"## ChatGPT / Codex: enable device-code auth first"},{"id":"p39s1","text":"[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p40s1","text":"## Compatibility update"},{"id":"p41s1","text":"- `@earendil-works/pi-ai` is `^1.5.0` (lockfile 1.5.0): the `openai`, `openai-codex` and `github-cop"},{"id":"p41s2","text":"ilot` catalogs include `gpt-6.1-terra`.\n- Reviewed against Harness `0.1.5-rc.2` (source commit `c291"},{"id":"p41s3","text":"e7961a`): leading system messages, selected reasoning efforts, and the `ToolCallId` rename are handl"},{"id":"p41s4","text":"ed. Older `CallId` exports remain supported.\n- Settings integration uses the `SettingsProvider.insta"},{"id":"p41s5","text":"llSection` service API; `deepEqualJson` comes from the host peer `@deepseek-ai/dsh-util-values`, avo"},{"id":"p41s6","text":"iding removed standalone exports from `dsh-settings`.\n- The lockfile no longer embeds third-party mi"},{"id":"p41s7","text":"rror tarball URLs. The project `.npmrc` selects the official npm registry, fixing issue #1. Normal G"},{"id":"p41s8","text":"it installs can run `prepare`; skipping scripts is not required."}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
